@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `il07-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il28-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-s48-area-order`
IMPORT `ito-s48a-foreign-worker-regs`
IMPORT `ito-il28-routing`

-- ===========================================================================
-- IL-07 adapter for row IL-28: ITO s 48 with the Area order of 5755-1995, and
-- ITO s 48A with the foreign worker Regulations of 5775-2014.
--
-- VERSION 0.6.0 (2026-10-09, BACKLOG IL-55). Imports this row's nouns and row
-- IL-28's modules (vendored copies, VENDORED.sha256), and no other row. It builds
-- row IL-28's `Taxpayer` from the household and the facts a caller adds (il07-
-- nouns.l4, `IL-07 the earner's facts under sections 48 and 48A of the Income Tax
-- Ordinance`), and returns row IL-28's points in place of ss 34, 36, 36A and 37
-- and what the instrument that reaches the earner does to a provision.
--
-- WHOM IT IS ASKED ABOUT. The pipeline asks it only of an earner the household
-- says is a foreign worker within s 48A, or a resident of the Area who is not an
-- Israeli citizen, who has no spouse, and for whom the caller adds the facts
-- (fork K25). Every other such earner is refused as before, in rows IL-01's and
-- IL-08's words ("section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in
-- this model"; "section 48 and the order made under it ...").
--
-- INPUT CONVENTIONS (assumed, not ruled: the lead's direction for IL-55):
-- * an individual; a woman, an Israeli resident in the tax year, a resident of the
--   Area, a foreign worker ("a worker"): the household's facts;
-- * income from personal exertion: the monthly salary is above nil (as for row
--   IL-01, NOTES.md section 14.3); the income taxed is income under s 2(2);
-- * the three facts of s 37: FALSE, since the earner has no spouse and s 37 is a
--   point for the maintenance of a spouse;
-- * the rest: the facts the caller adds.
-- The readings: row IL-28's own switches, but fork F1 (s 36A and residence) as
-- the capstone names it for rows IL-01 and IL-02, one question for all three.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `IL-07 adapter — row IL-28`

@ref ITO s 3A(a), s 48, s 48A (row IL-28, ito-il28-nouns.l4, `Taxpayer`); the Foreign Workers Law s 1; REG 1-3; the input conventions above
GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      x IS AN `IL-07 the earner's facts under sections 48 and 48A of the Income Tax Ordinance`
GIVETH A Taxpayer
`IL-28: the earner as a taxpayer, in` h `, with the facts` x MEANS
    Taxpayer WITH
        `the tax year`                                           IS h's `the year of the month`
        `an individual`                                          IS TRUE
        `a woman`                                                IS e's `the earner is a woman`
        `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                    IS e's `the earner was an Israeli resident in the tax year, under the Income Tax Ordinance`
        `a resident of the Area`                                 IS e's `the earner is a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen`
        `an Israeli citizen under the Citizenship Law`           IS x's `the earner is an Israeli citizen under the Citizenship Law`
        `entitled to immigrate under the Law of Return`          IS x's `the earner is entitled to immigrate under the Law of Return`
        `the taxpayer's residence in the Area over the tax year` IS
            CONSIDER x's `the months of the tax year in which the earner was a resident of the Area, if not the whole year`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the Area residence entered held for the whole tax year`
            WHEN JUST m  THEN `a resident of the Area for only part of the tax year` m
        `a favoured individual within section 37`                IS FALSE
        `the spouse's livelihood was upon the taxpayer`          IS FALSE
        `the taxpayer proved it to the assessor's satisfaction`  IS FALSE
        `the taxpayer had income from personal exertion in the tax year` IS e's `the earner's monthly salary` GREATER THAN 0
        `a worker`                                               IS e's `the earner is a foreign worker`
        `a resident of Israel within the Foreign Workers Law`    IS x's `the earner is a resident of Israel within the Foreign Workers Law`
        `holds a visa under section 2 of the Entry into Israel Law, or needs one` IS x's `the earner holds a visa under section 2 of the Entry into Israel Law, or needs one`
        `stay in Israel or the Area and employment there are permitted by law` IS x's `the earner's stay in Israel or the Area and employment there are permitted by law`
        `an expert from abroad or a guest lecturer`              IS x's `the earner is an expert from abroad or a guest lecturer`
        `holds a B/1 temporary worker visa and licence`          IS x's `the earner holds a B/1 temporary worker visa and licence`
        `holds a permit to work in the caring sector`            IS x's `the earner holds a permit to work in the caring sector`
        `the stay is extended under section 3A(b) of the Entry into Israel Law` IS x's `the earner's stay is extended under section 3A(b) of the Entry into Israel Law`
        `the months of the tax year spent in Israel or the Area` IS x's `the months of the tax year the earner spent in Israel or the Area`
        `the income taxed is income under section 2(1) or (2)`   IS TRUE
    WHERE
        e MEANS h's `the earner`

@ref Meng's ruling SHRUG, 2026-10-08 (row IL-28, ito-il28-routing.l4, `the readings this row takes`); fork F1 as the capstone names it (il07-nouns.l4)
GIVEN r IS AN `IL-07 the readings of the composed rows' forks`
GIVETH A `The readings of the forks of row IL-28`
`IL-28: its readings, for` r MEANS
    `The readings of the forks of row IL-28` WITH
        `fork F1, section 36A and residence`                    IS
            CONSIDER r's `section 36A on residence (row IL-01 fork F1, row IL-02 fork F20)`
            WHEN `IL-07: section 36A at the rows' own switches, declined where residence decides it` THEN `declined where residence decides section 36A`
            WHEN `IL-07: section 36A without a residence condition`                                  THEN `section 36A has no residence condition`
            WHEN `IL-07: section 36A only for an Israeli resident`                                   THEN `section 36A gives its half point only to an Israeli resident`
        `fork F2, section 36 and income from personal exertion` IS `declined where income from personal exertion decides section 36`
        `fork F4, residence in the Area for part of a tax year` IS `declined for residence in part of a tax year`
        `fork FW1, the cited sections' conditions`              IS `declined where the cited sections' residence conditions decide`
        `fork FW2, the tax years from 2002 to 2014`             IS `declined for the tax years from 2002 to 2014`
        `fork FW3, regulation 3(d) and deductions`              IS `declined where regulation 3(d) and the chapter's deductions meet`
        `fork OV, both instruments reach the taxpayer`          IS `declined where the order and the regulations both reach the taxpayer`

-- Row IL-28's points in place of ss 34, 36, 36A and 37 (the Order's, or reg 3's).
@ref ITO ss 48, 48A; ORD s 1; REG 3 (row IL-28, ito-il28-routing.l4, `the total credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for`)
GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      x IS AN `IL-07 the earner's facts under sections 48 and 48A of the Income Tax Ordinance`
      r IS AN `IL-07 the readings of the composed rows' forks`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-28: the credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for the earner, in` h `, with the facts` x `, reading` r MEANS
    `the total credit points in place of sections 34, 36, 36A and 37 for` (`IL-28: the earner as a taxpayer, in` h `, with the facts` x) `, under` (`IL-28: its readings, for` r)

-- Whether the instrument that reaches the earner takes away a credit or deduction
-- of the chapter (TRUE), leaves it to its own section (FALSE), or the row declines
-- (its fork FW3 for ss 47 and 47A, at its default). Row IL-28's other effects
-- ("applies the provision as if …", "gives the provision a partial effect") are of
-- ss 34, 36, 36A and 37, whose points the rule above gives.
@ref ITO ss 48, 48A; ORD s 1; REG 3(d) (row IL-28, ito-il28-routing.l4, `what the instrument that reaches`)
GIVEN p IS A `A provision of Chapter Three`
      h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      x IS AN `IL-07 the earner's facts under sections 48 and 48A of the Income Tax Ordinance`
      r IS AN `IL-07 the readings of the composed rows' forks`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IL-28: the instrument that reaches the earner takes away` p `, in` h `, with the facts` x `, reading` r MEANS
    CONSIDER `what the instrument that reaches` (`IL-28: the earner as a taxpayer, in` h `, with the facts` x) `, under` (`IL-28: its readings, for` r) `, does to` p
    WHEN `disapplies the provision` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The provisions the pipeline asks about, by name (row IL-28's constructors).
GIVETH A `A provision of Chapter Three`
`IL-28: section 35` MEANS `section 35`
GIVETH A `A provision of Chapter Three`
`IL-28: section 40` MEANS `section 40`
GIVETH A `A provision of Chapter Three`
`IL-28: section 45A` MEANS `section 45A`
GIVETH A `A provision of Chapter Three`
`IL-28: section 47` MEANS `section 47, a deduction`
